    "raw_reply": "A\nChief Technology Officer (CTO)\nis a top executive in charge of a company's technology strategy and engineering, but\nthey are not always the direct head of everyday internal IT operations\nCTO vs. Head of IT (CIO)\nThe CTO:\nFocuses outward and forward. They drive research, build tech products or software for customers, and plan long-term innovation.\nForbes\nThe Head of IT (often the CIO or Chief Information Officer):\nFocuses inward. They manage internal computer systems, employee help desks, day-to-day networks, and internal software.\nWhen the CTO Runs IT\nIn smaller companies or startups, one person often handles both roles.\nThe CTO might oversee the IT department simply because there is no separate CIO or IT Director.\nChief technology officer - Wikipedia\nA chief technology officer (CTO), chief technical officer, or chief technologist is a corporate officer tasked with managing techn...\nInvestopedia\nChief Technology Officer (CTO): Key Responsibilities and Role\nA chief technology officer (CTO) is a high-ranking executive who manages a company's technology and engineering departments. CTOs ...\nForbes\nWhat Is A Chief Technology Officer? CTO Role Explained\nA chief technology officer (CTO) is the head of technology for an organization. They are responsible for: * **Managing IT and data...\nIndeed\nWhat Is a CTO (Chief Technology Officer)? (Plus Salary) | Indeed.com\nKEY TAKEAWAYS: * A Chief Technology Officer (CTO) is responsible for overseeing the development and distribution of technology to ...\nEvidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) - Evidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) * Key responsibilities. Technology strategy: Develops long-term plans for technology growth and inn...\nChief technology officer - Wikipedia\nA chief technology officer (CTO), chief technical officer, or chief technologist is a corporate officer tasked with managing techn...\nInvestopedia\nChief Technology Officer (CTO): Key Responsibilities and Role\nA chief technology officer (CTO) is a high-ranking executive who manages a company's technology and engineering departments. CTOs ...\nForbes\nWhat Is A Chief Technology Officer? CTO Role Explained\nA chief technology officer (CTO) is the head of technology for an organization. They are responsible for: * **Managing IT and data...\nIndeed\nWhat Is a CTO (Chief Technology Officer)? (Plus Salary) | Indeed.com\nKEY TAKEAWAYS: * A Chief Technology Officer (CTO) is responsible for overseeing the development and distribution of technology to ...\nEvidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) - Evidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) * Key responsibilities. Technology strategy: Develops long-term plans for technology growth and inn...\nShow less",
