    "raw_reply": "A Head of Technology is often the same as a Chief Technology Officer (CTO) in smaller companies\n, but they are distinct roles in larger organizations.\nSplunk\nKey Differences\nExecutive Level:\nA\nCTO\nis a C-suite executive who sets the high-level, long-term technical vision and aligns it with business goals. A Head of Technology usually reports to the CTO or another executive and focuses on execution.\nDaily Operations:\nA Head of Technology manages day-to-day tech operations, projects, and engineering teams. A CTO focuses on strategy, external products, and innovation rather than daily management.\nEvidi\nCompany Size:\nIn startups or mid-sized firms, the titles are used interchangeably because one person handles both strategy and daily operations\n. In large enterprises, the CTO plans the future while the Head of Technology runs the current systems.\nSplunk\nChief technology officer - Wikipedia\nA chief technology officer (CTO), chief technical officer, or chief technologist is a corporate officer tasked with managing techn...\nSplunk\nThe Chief Technology Officer Role: Skills, Responsibilities, and Career ...\nCTO vs. CIO vs CPO: What's the difference? The CIO (Chief Information Officer) handles internal IT infrastructure and operations a...\nZipRecruiter\nWhat is the difference between Head Of Technology vs CTO? - ZipRecruiter\nThe Head Of Technology typically manages day-to-day tech operations and teams, focusing on project execution. The CTO holds a stra...\nEvidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) - Evidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) * Key responsibilities. Technology strategy: Develops long-term plans for technology growth and inn...\nChief technology officer - Wikipedia\nA chief technology officer (CTO), chief technical officer, or chief technologist is a corporate officer tasked with managing techn...\nSplunk\nThe Chief Technology Officer Role: Skills, Responsibilities, and Career ...\nCTO vs. CIO vs CPO: What's the difference? The CIO (Chief Information Officer) handles internal IT infrastructure and operations a...\nZipRecruiter\nWhat is the difference between Head Of Technology vs CTO? - ZipRecruiter\nThe Head Of Technology typically manages day-to-day tech operations and teams, focusing on project execution. The CTO holds a stra...\nEvidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) - Evidi\nChief Technology Officer (CTO) * Key responsibilities. Technology strategy: Develops long-term plans for technology growth and inn...\nShow less",
    "error": ""
  },
